laurel mu 0002: NegroniBootMemoryDxe logs each DT memory bank (NEGRONIMEM: DT memory bank 0x..-0x..), so the UEFI screen
log shows the DDR banks ABL wrote into the live FDT (the Mi A3 has 6 GB; the 2026-11-01 boot showed only the holes it added).
Applied to external/Mu-Silicium-negroni by scripts/laurel/mu-build.sh (shared with negroniPkg, harmless there).
diff --git a/Platforms/OnePlus/negroniPkg/Drivers/NegroniBootMemoryDxe/NegroniBootMemoryDxe.c b/Platforms/OnePlus/negroniPkg/Drivers/NegroniBootMemoryDxe/NegroniBootMemoryDxe.c
index e1a1c298..affd9d85 100644
--- a/Platforms/OnePlus/negroniPkg/Drivers/NegroniBootMemoryDxe/NegroniBootMemoryDxe.c
+++ b/Platforms/OnePlus/negroniPkg/Drivers/NegroniBootMemoryDxe/NegroniBootMemoryDxe.c
@@ -184,6 +184,9 @@ AddMemory (
   }
 
   DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "NEGRONIMEM: DT has %u memory ranges and %u reserved ranges\n", (UINT32)BankCount, (UINT32)ReservedCount));
+  for (Index = 0; Index < BankCount; Index++) {
+    DEBUG ((DEBUG_ERROR, "NEGRONIMEM: DT memory bank 0x%lx-0x%lx\n", Banks[Index].Base, Banks[Index].End - 1));
+  }
   if (BankCount == 0) {
     return;
   }
